en:
Ah, I see.
So you only know the name.
It seems quite a lot of people are like that.{p}

A senior from the newspaper club...
Hino, I believe his name was?
When he invited me to this seven wonders gathering, I thanked my lucky stars.{p}

You're saying we should wait a little longer?
You have quite a persistent nature.
Just what I'd expect from a newspaper club member.{p}

Down...!
Thinking that on instinct, I rushed down the stairs.
...But then,{p}

A black shadow seemed to spread slowly across the backs of my eyelids.
A shadow like a black cloak spread wide...
Was this the Three O'Clock Phantom...?{p}

"{a}... {a}..."
Someone was calling me......
...Arai's voice?{p}

"Yes...
I didn't see it clearly, but right after I fell down the stairs, I think I saw a black shadow."
I answered, pulling together the threads of my hazy memory.{p}

The Three O'Clock Hag is said to be a yokai that appears in restrooms at exactly three in the afternoon, isn't it?
People hearing a hoarse voice...
A stain shaped like an old woman appearing on the wall...{p}

From what I've heard, the Three O'Clock Hag is a yokai that appears in restrooms at exactly three in the afternoon.
Then again...
All that gets passed around are stories of someone hearing a hoarse voice, or of a stain shaped like an old woman appearing on the wall. It seems no one has ever actually seen the yokai itself.{p}

A student on the track team that Coach Adachi advised killed himself.
He jumped from the school roof in the middle of the night.
His broken wristwatch had stopped, still pointing to three.{p}

And from that time on, the rumor of the Three O'Clock Phantom began to spread.
Some people said the Phantom was really Coach Adachi, while others said it was the track team student who had killed himself.
There really are so many rumors going around, you see...{p}

Ah, everyone's nodding.
...Otherwise, none of you could be here right now.
Just what I'd expect from people chosen by Hino. You're a well-informed bunch.{p}

Because the first thing that matters in the ritual is to 'linger'... to wait...
But, {a}.
That's not all there is to it.{p}

Everyone looks dissatisfied.
...It's all right.
Later, I'll teach you all a way to settle that dissatisfaction.{p}

Linger...
Indulge...
Ea......{p}

...It's almost three now.
Linger, indulge, Ea...
Good, I haven't forgotten.{p}

{a}...
What are you dawdling for?
Come on, hurry up and move the hands.{p}

There, that's all it takes.
You heard it too, didn't you?
There was definitely a click just now, wasn't there?{p}

Still, what bothers me is...
Why would the newspaper club entrust the seven wonders interviews to someone like you?
...I can only think it was plain spite.{p}

{a}...
The truth is, they hate you, don't they?
Forgive me for kicking you while you're down, but I do believe the Phantom will appear.{p}

{a}...
I don't know that either.
But I believe the Phantom will appear.{p}

Since these are the seven wonders, I wanted to let you write a wonderful article, {a}!
That's why I tried to summon the Three O'Clock Phantom.
But the Phantom didn't appear.{p}

"Don't say that, please set them.
All right?
Here we go.{p}

Ba-dump...!
I felt as if my heart was being crushed in someone's fist.
Because I understood painfully well what he meant.{p}
